.TH MCXEDIT 1 (unknown-date) "mcxedit (unknown-version)"
.SH NAME
mcxedit \- utility for processing "Minecraft: Java Edition" Region files

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcxedit
.RI [ OPTIONS ]\~ FILE ...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcxedit
is a tool used to edit regioud files for your "Minecraft: Java Edition" worlds.
This is useful for reducing world size, general world management, copying chunks
from one world to another, or various other administrative tasks.

.SH OPTIONS

\" TODO: Document further options
\" API as of now is too unstable to make any final decisions on what
\" these options should be or do.

.TP
.B -q
Silences non-fatal errors.

.TP
.B -v
Prints the software version
and prints more verbose information about the files.

.TP
.B -h
Shows a brief explanation on the options available.
Adding potentially useful mnemonics.

.TP
.B --
End of options, remaining arguments are treated as file paths.

.SH EXIT STATUS
0 is on success, 1 if any of
.IR FILE "... had an issue,"
.RI "in which case an error is (usually) printed to " stderr .
